  "response_text": "If a queue is used to store the thread control blocks, the currently running queue would be dequeued from the front, and after it yields, it would be requeued at the back. This would allow for the implementation of round robin scheduling because the scheduler would just pick the next thread to run by dequeuing the front of the queue. The benefit to this approach is that the scheduling logic would be simpler than an array with index tracking, especially if threads were to be added or removed. This is because the queue automatically handles order preservation and cycling, and it avoids the need for manual index and stack pointer management.\\n",
